      "id": "LZF-05",
      "title": "The continued Euler identity and its use in the chain",
      "statement": "A good-place insertion multiplies the restricted integral by L_v(s+1/2)/d_v(s). On Re(s)>a+1 the full integral equals L^S(s+1/2) J_S(s)/d^S(s). Continuation gives the special-value identity at t/2. A nonzero holomorphic L-value with the chosen tests forces the upward lift to be nonzero.",
